--- !u!114 &1299823326
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1299823325}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f1af3d7c73bf92647908bce9110a0af3, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::PhaseTransitionManager
  useMarkerArrow: 1
  promptLines:
  - text: "Good work \u2014 you've handled every hazard in this Kitchen"
    characterPose: {fileID: 21300000, guid: dc86be78c176b7249911c3e5eec98bf6, type: 3}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 0}
  - text: But knowing what causes a fire is only half of it. You also need to know
      what to do when one actually starts.
    characterPose: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 2cb2c185d83af914aa26b4c0fb08c86f, type: 3}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Look for the wet blanket. Go to it.
    characterPose: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 2cb2c185d83af914aa26b4c0fb08c86f, type: 3}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 0}
  teachTarget1: {fileID: 1625928391}
  teach1Lines:
  - text: This is an ordinary kitchen towel. Wet it, and it becomes the safest thing
      you can reach for.
    characterPose: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 1df00db9a1101574d87e2b5df19761c5, type: 3}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 0}
  - text: The fire here is gas. It is leaking from the worn hose at the regulator
      and burning as it escapes.
    characterPose: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6dabcd07478f38b4384467fb682f154c, type: 3}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Fire needs air. A wet towel laid over the flame takes the air away, and
      the flame goes out.
    characterPose: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6dabcd07478f38b4384467fb682f154c, type: 3}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Wet it, then wring it out. A dripping towel splashes, and steam near a
      gas flame will burn your hands.
    characterPose: {fileID: 0}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Lay it down. Do not throw it. A thrown towel fans the flame and can knock
      the hose loose.
    characterPose: {fileID: 0}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Leave it in place. Lifting it to check lets the air back in, and gas relights
      instantly.
    characterPose: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 2cb2c185d83af914aa26b4c0fb08c86f, type: 3}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 0}
  - text: "But the towel only kills the flame \u2014 the gas is still leaking underneath
      it. Look at the tank valve. That is what actually ends this."
    characterPose: {fileID: 21300000, guid: dc86be78c176b7249911c3e5eec98bf6, type: 3}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 0}
  teachTarget2: {fileID: 0}
  teach2Lines:
  - text: "This is a fire extinguisher. But here's something most people don't know
      \u2014 not every extinguisher works on every fire."
    characterPose: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 1df00db9a1101574d87e2b5df19761c5, type: 3}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 0}
  - text: "In an office, two kinds of fire are most likely. Paper and furniture burning
      \u2014 that's Class A. And electrical fires from wiring or equipment \u2014
      that's Class C."
    characterPose: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6dabcd07478f38b4384467fb682f154c, type: 3}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 0}
  - text: That's why offices use an ABC extinguisher, like this one. It handles paper,
      liquids, and electrical fires all in one.
    characterPose: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6dabcd07478f38b4384467fb682f154c, type: 3}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 0}
  - text: "Never throw water on an electrical fire. Water carries electricity \u2014
      it can travel right back to you through the stream."
    characterPose: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6dabcd07478f38b4384467fb682f154c, type: 3}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Now, how to use it. Remember the word TPASS. Five steps, in order.
    characterPose: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6dabcd07478f38b4384467fb682f154c, type: 3}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 0}
  - text: "T \u2014 Twist. Twist the safety pin to break the plastic seal."
    characterPose: {fileID: 21300000, guid: af31bd5f2944a0a49a02e7aa930fe642, type: 3}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 1e78d9f77641a64408f5e6b5239edce5, type: 3}
  - text: "P \u2014 Pull. Pull the pin straight out. The extinguisher is now ready."
    characterPose: {fileID: 21300000, guid: af31bd5f2944a0a49a02e7aa930fe642, type: 3}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 1e78d9f77641a64408f5e6b5239edce5, type: 3}
  - text: "A \u2014 Aim. Point the nozzle at the bottom of the fire, not the flames.
      The fuel is at the base \u2014 that's what you need to put out."
    characterPose: {fileID: 21300000, guid: af31bd5f2944a0a49a02e7aa930fe642, type: 3}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 1e78d9f77641a64408f5e6b5239edce5, type: 3}
  - text: "S \u2014 Squeeze. Squeeze the handle to release the spray. Keep a firm
      grip."
    characterPose: {fileID: 21300000, guid: af31bd5f2944a0a49a02e7aa930fe642, type: 3}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 1e78d9f77641a64408f5e6b5239edce5, type: 3}
  - text: "S \u2014 Sweep. Move the nozzle side to side across the base until the
      fire is out."
    characterPose: {fileID: 21300000, guid: af31bd5f2944a0a49a02e7aa930fe642, type: 3}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 1e78d9f77641a64408f5e6b5239edce5, type: 3}
  - text: "You've completed the learning module. What comes next is a real \r\nscenario
      \u2014 timed, and without guidance. Everything you need, you \r\nalready know.
      Ready?"
    characterPose: {fileID: 21300000, guid: dc86be78c176b7249911c3e5eec98bf6, type: 3}
    demoVideo: {fileID: 0}
  confirmPanel: {fileID: 680703511}
  loadingTagline: PREPARING SIMULATION
